deslop — third-party acknowledgements
=====================================

deslop is original work (MIT, see LICENSE). The AI-writing pattern taxonomy
and the human/AI signals it scores draw on the following prior work, none of
which is redistributed here verbatim:

1. stop-slop — https://github.com/hardikpandya/stop-slop  (MIT)
   The English "slop" pattern catalogue that inspired deslop's approach.
   deslop's Korean and English pattern sets were reimagined and reimplemented
   as deterministic transforms; no stop-slop source text is copied.

2. "Signs of AI writing" — Wikipedia editing guide  (CC BY-SA 4.0)
   Used as a reference when compiling the pattern descriptions in PATTERNS.md.
   PATTERNS.md prose that paraphrases this guide is noted there; see PATTERNS.md.

3. KatFishNet / KatFish — "Detecting LLM-Generated Korean Text through
   Linguistic Feature Analysis", ACL 2025 (arXiv:2503.00032)
   Cited as the source for the observation that Korean-specific signals
   (spacing, POS diversity, comma usage) help separate machine-written Korean
   text. deslop reuses none of its code or dataset; it is a citation only.

